# LLM CLI workflow

## Project

Cross-platform local AI runtime manager (.NET 8). Windows-first; targets llama.cpp with Vulkan (Intel Iris Xe).

## Before finishing any coding turn

Update `.cursor/workflow/CHANGELOG.md` under `[Unreleased]` (newest first).

Run `.\scripts\harness.ps1` before marking a phase complete.

## Build & test (required)

```powershell
dotnet build LLM.sln
dotnet test
```

Every change must compile with 0 errors. Prefer 0 warnings.

## Architecture rules

- **LLM.CLI** — commands, services, configuration; no business logic in `Program.cs` beyond DI wiring.
- **LLM.Core** — routing foundation only; no Microsoft.Extensions dependency in Core.
- **User config** — `%LOCALAPPDATA%\LLM\config.json` (settings only).
- **Workspace** — user-chosen root (e.g. `D:\AI`) holds runtimes, models, logs.
- **Managed runtime** — `<workspace>\runtimes\llama.cpp\current\` (copied via `runtime import`, never symlink to source build).

## Command conventions

- Flat dispatcher today: `llm runtime status` passes `["runtime", "status"]` to nested handlers.
- New commands: implement `ICommand`, register in `Program.cs`, update `HelpCommand`.
- Config keys use `Runtime:Model`, `Runtime:Port`, `Runtime:GpuLayers` (case-insensitive in handler).

## Runtime defaults (Snigdho hardware)

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| GpuLayers | 29 |
| ContextSize | 16384 |
| Threads | 8 |
| Port | 8080 |
| Backend | Vulkan via ggml-vulkan.dll |

## Do not

- Hardcode `C:\llama.cpp` or `D:\MODEL` in source — use config.
- Modify appsettings.json at runtime — use user config.
- Add duplicate `ICommand` interfaces (CLI uses `LLM.CLI.Commands.ICommand` until router migration).

## Commit message style

```
feat(runtime): import local llama.cpp build into workspace
fix(config): normalize root directory on load
docs(workflow): add Cursor development guide
```

## Next priorities

1. Hugging Face model catalog (`model search`, `model pull`)
2. Auto runtime management (`llm serve`, restart on profile change)
3. Migrate to `LLM.Core.Routing.CommandRouter` when command count grows
